1
00:00:00,919 --> 00:00:10,474
Welcome to the Asia capitals, episode three of seven. First, I clear the
chosen names for a fresh regional lesson.

2
00:00:11,136 --> 00:00:22,142
Seven capitals of South Asia: the two planned capitals of the north, the Hindu
Kush, the Himalaya, the Bengal delta and the island of Sri Lanka.

3
00:00:22,805 --> 00:00:24,802
Let's bring New Delhi into view.

4
00:00:29,001 --> 00:00:38,173
New Delhi stands on the Yamuna river in north-central India, about fifteen
kilometres from the older city of Delhi.

5
00:00:38,823 --> 00:00:51,954
Planned by the architects Edwin Lutyens and Herbert Baker and inaugurated in
1931, its Rashtrapati Bhavan, the president's palace, has some 340 rooms.

6
00:00:52,611 --> 00:01:01,655
Remember New Delhi as the planned garden capital of 1931, with India Gate for
the soldiers of the First World War.

7
00:01:02,342 --> 00:01:05,883
Let's bring Islamabad into view.

8
00:01:08,394 --> 00:01:16,788
Islamabad was built in the 1960s as a new capital at the foot of the Margalla
Hills, in the north of Pakistan.

9
00:01:17,445 --> 00:01:27,383
Its Faisal Mosque, shaped like a desert tent, was for years the largest in the
world, and its twin city Rawalpindi lies right next to it.

10
00:01:28,054 --> 00:01:35,682
Remember Islamabad as the new tent-shaped mosque capital of the 1960s, beside
its twin city.

11
00:01:36,445 --> 00:01:38,105
Let's bring Kabul into view.

12
00:01:46,937 --> 00:01:54,948
Kabul lies in a valley among the mountains of the Hindu Kush, in the east of
Afghanistan, at about 1,800 metres.

13
00:01:55,612 --> 00:02:02,172
Babur, the founder of the Mughal empire, asked to be buried here, and his
garden tomb still stands.

14
00:02:02,836 --> 00:02:10,719
Remember Kabul as the high valley capital where Babur asked to be buried, and
one of the highest capitals in the world.

15
00:02:11,471 --> 00:02:13,468
Let's bring Kathmandu into view.

16
00:02:22,965 --> 00:02:30,848
Kathmandu stands in a valley north of the Himalayas, in the centre of Nepal,
at about 1,400 metres.

17
00:02:31,510 --> 00:02:40,717
From Kasthamandap, a temple said to have been built from the wood of a single
tree, its Durbar Square belongs to the valley's UNESCO site.

18
00:02:41,376 --> 00:02:48,412
Remember Kathmandu as the temple of a single tree, with the stupa of
Swayambhunath on its hill.

19
00:02:49,099 --> 00:02:51,317
Let's bring Thimphu into view.

20
00:02:56,535 --> 00:03:04,000
Thimphu lies in a valley in the north of Bhutan, on the Wang Chhu river below
the mountains that ring the kingdom.

21
00:03:04,658 --> 00:03:12,971
A capital without traffic lights: police officers direct the traffic by hand.
It became the capital in 1961.

22
00:03:13,633 --> 00:03:21,226
Remember Thimphu as the capital with no traffic lights, its police waving cars
through the valley by hand.

23
00:03:21,906 --> 00:03:24,588
Let's bring Dhaka into view.

24
00:03:28,627 --> 00:03:36,382
Dhaka stands on the Buriganga river in the centre of Bangladesh, in the delta
of the Ganges, Brahmaputra and Meghna.

25
00:03:37,038 --> 00:03:44,921
Often called the rickshaw capital of the world, it is one of the most densely
populated cities in the world.

26
00:03:45,577 --> 00:03:54,702
Remember Dhaka as the rickshaw capital of the delta, with Louis Kahn's
parliament house of 1982.

27
00:03:55,373 --> 00:03:58,055
Let's bring Colombo into view.

28
00:04:01,379 --> 00:04:12,850
Colombo stands on the west coast of Sri Lanka, on the shore facing the Indian
Ocean; the official capital, Sri Jayawardenepura Kotte, lies on its edge.

29
00:04:13,507 --> 00:04:24,467
Its seaside park, Galle Face Green, dates from 1859, and Arab traders knew its
harbour centuries before the Portuguese arrived in 1505.

30
00:04:25,119 --> 00:04:33,119
Remember Colombo as the commercial capital on the Indian Ocean, with a harbour
known to Arab traders long before the Portuguese.

31
00:04:38,362 --> 00:04:53,757
New Delhi and Islamabad are the twentieth-century planned capitals, with Kabul
in the Hindu Kush between them. Kathmandu and Thimphu are the Himalayan
valleys, Dhaka the delta, and Colombo the ocean port.

32
00:04:54,415 --> 00:05:11,983
Remember the garden capital of 1931, the tent-shaped mosque, Babur's tomb, the
temple of a single tree, the capital with no traffic lights, the rickshaw
capital, and the harbour Arab traders knew first.
